    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d41">

                <pb facs="0153" n="115" xml:id="pg115"/>

                <head>41. Memorandum of a Conversation Between Prime Minister Mollet and Secretary
                    of State Dulles, Washington, February 26, 1957<anchor n="1" xml:id="d41-f1"
                    /></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                ><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                                type="conversation-or-meeting-date" when="1957-02-26">February 26,
                                1957</date></hi></dateline></opener>
                <p>At the dinner<anchor n="2" xml:id="d41-f2"/> I gave for Mollet I spoke to him
                    about French intentions with respect to nuclear weapons. He said that so far as
                    he personally was concerned he would never approve of France going into this.
                    However, he felt that France should reserve the right to do so.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
